findings.surviving_mutation:
In ChainReplay.replayAncestry's neverOpened branch, replace
    if (chainEpoch >= 1 && crossFromCheckpoint(hops, chainEpoch, limit)) { break; }
    if (chainEpoch >= 1) { hops.add(new Hop(chainEpoch, 0, limit)); }
with
    if (chainEpoch >= 1) { crossFromCheckpoint(hops, chainEpoch, limit); hops.add(new Hop(chainEpoch, 0, limit)); }
i.e. probe the checkpoint, fold its offsets, and then walk the whole ancestry anyway. MEASURED in my own tree: 298 tests, 0 failures. The sentinel 500 survives because `crossFromCheckpoint` merges with `Math::max` and the deltas only reach 4, so the offset assertion cannot tell 'stopped here' from 'folded it in and kept walking'.
